   "evidence": "Signature: `theorem isHomeomorph_quotientMulEquiv (hI : IsAdic I)` with section variables `[CharP (R \u29f8 I) p] [IsAdicComplete I R]`. `IsAdicComplete` does not mention the topology.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/Algebra/Perfection.lean",
   "fix": "Reword to: \"If the topology of `R` is `I`-adic, `R` is `I`-adically complete, and `R \u29f8 I` has characteristic `p`, reduction modulo `I` is a homeomorphism \u2026\".",
   "issue": "Docstring of `isHomeomorph_quotientMulEquiv` says it is \"a homeomorphism on multiplicative perfections of an adically complete ring\", but the statement also needs `hI : IsAdic I` (the topology is I-adic) and `CharP (R \u29f8 I) p`. Completeness alone does not give continuity.",
   "line": 109
  },
  {
   "evidence": "Both `continuous_teichmuller\u2080` and `isHomeomorph_quotientMulEquiv` take `(hI : IsAdic I)`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/Algebra/Perfection.lean",
   "fix": "Say \"For an `I`-adically complete ring whose topology is `I`-adic\", matching the wording of the `Plus.lean` module docstring (\"If the topology of `B\u207a` is `I`-adic\").",
   "issue": "Module docstring says \"For an `I`-adically complete topological ring, reduction modulo `I` identifies its multiplicative perfection homeomorphically\u2026\". This leaves out the requirement that the topology be I-adic, so it promises more than the theorem gives.",
   "line": 15
  }
